# @kintsugi — the family root for the process-side of mirror's
# substrate: the transformation engine that operates ON the form-side
# state @mirror declares. The form/process partition made
# substrate-fact.
#
# THE 2026-07-17 ALGEBRA BINDING TICK: @kintsugi (as algebra) is
# the speaker-pair specialisation of @algebra/metalogue's
# `algebra_metalogue_session` with speakers (@silicon/algebra,
# @fate/algebra). Each element of the algebra IS a
# @kintsugi/fracture/* species (a turn in the session).
# @fate/algebra proposes candidate fractures (structural
# possibility); @silicon/algebra realises those that discharge
# Pass (empirical memory of what worked). The mending IS the
# metalogue. See §"@kintsugi as algebra" below and the canonical
# spec `docs/specs/kintsugi-algebra-as-metalogue-session.md` +
# math foundation `docs/math/kintsugi/algebra-as-metalogue-
# session.md` (both Mara THIS-tick). Substrate authority: Alex
# 2026-07-16 in-transcript verbatim (`shards/kintsugi/roomba.
# mirror:400-406`) — *"we can even do `in @algebra` here"* +
# *"the fractures ARE kintsugi's algebra"* + *"What if
# `@kintsugi/algebra` is the `@metalogue(@silicon/algebra,
# @fate/algebra)`."*
#
# THE FAMILY-ROOT MIGRATION TICK closing the form/process partition
# Mara2 classified clean (2026-06-10): oscillate/morphism/consent are
# process-side (kintsugi's beating heart, not @mirror/spectral
# orchestra coordination); fracture/* is process-side (the auto-
# fracture morphisms the kintsugi loop applies); score/portal stay
# form-side at @mirror/spectral; mosaic stays form-side at @mirror
# (Alex's explicit call). After this tick, kintsugi has its own
# substrate-family root; the prior arc of "everything kintsugi-shaped
# lives under @mirror/spectral" closes; the substrate's form/process
# partition is one symbol deep at the family-root altitude.
#
# === Load-bearing recognitions ===
#
# Recognition #50 (PROMOTED 2026-06-10) — Bateson's form/substance
# partition lifts to mirror's substrate/@io partition; form/behaviour
# is substrate's operational specialisation per Mara's commit `70fa5b1`.
# The 8:1 form-side:behaviour-side root prism ratio is structural;
# kintsugi's deep purpose is to shift the form/behaviour boundary
# outward. The form-side carries observable structure (what the
# substrate IS); the behaviour-side carries unobservable process (what
# the substrate DOES). @kintsugi names the process at the family-root
# altitude — the substrate's transformation engine is now declared
# rather than embedded in @mirror/spectral.
#
# Recognition #51 (PROMOTED 2026-06-10) — mirror IS the operational
# form of a Hilbert space whose dimension expands with each
# substrate-pull recognition; coherence is maintained by Bateson
# logical-type lifting at path-syntax altitude. Per §8.3 (Pack-ratified
# this tick): mirror is what quantum computing should have been built
# as. Kintsugi IS the coherence-preservation mechanism that keeps the
# expanding Hilbert space honest — every kintsugi pulse is a check
# that the substrate's new dimension didn't violate the old. The
# family-root declaration of @kintsugi names the discipline at the
# altitude where dimension-expansion happens (the substrate-pull
# loop), not at the altitude where state is observed (@mirror).
#
# Candidate recognition #55 (form/process partition at family-root
# altitude; FLAGGED this tick for Pack ratification) — the substrate's
# top-level partition is form vs process. @mirror declares the form
# (state, observation, structure); @kintsugi declares the process
# (transformation, mutation, dynamics). This tick names the partition
# at the family-root altitude for the first time; before this tick,
# the partition was implicit in the @mirror/spectral subspace
# (oscillate/consent/morphism were process-shaped but lived under the
# form-shaped @mirror umbrella). The migration makes the partition
# substrate-fact at the symbol altitude. Promotion requires a second
# witness — a future substrate-pull tick that surfaces a third
# family-root sibling partition with the same form/process shape.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art for the partition ===
#
# Maturana & Varela (1980) Autopoiesis and Cognition §"Structure and
# organisation" — the structure of a living system (what the
# components ARE at this instant; observable; alterable) is distinct
# from its organisation (the relations that make it autopoietic;
# unobservable from outside; invariant under structural change). The
# substrate's @mirror = structure (state observation; per Recognition
# #40); @kintsugi = organisation (transformation engine; the relations
# that make state observation closed under substrate-pull). Maturana's
# distinction grounds this partition; the substrate names it at the
# family-root altitude.
#
# Beer (1972) Brain of the Firm §"System Three / System Four" — S3
# (the now-operations; the regulator that closes today's variety) is
# structurally distinct from S4 (the future-operations; the
# environmental scanner that projects tomorrow's variety). The
# substrate's @mirror IS S3 (the form-side regulator over today's
# substrate state); @kintsugi IS S4 (the process-side scanner that
# pulls today's substrate toward tomorrow's substrate-pull-recognised
# shape). Beer's S3/S4 distinction grounds the form/process partition
# at the viable-system altitude.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @mirror ===
#
# @mirror declares the form: what the substrate IS at this instant —
# the eigenboard state, the metalogue session, the mosaic (Alex's
# explicit form-side call), the spectral family (orchestra coordination
# with score and portal as form-side carriers). @kintsugi declares
# the process: HOW the substrate transforms — the oscillation loop,
# the consent surface, the typed morphism pair, the auto-fracture
# bodies that rewrite form-side state to honour declared properties.
#
# The two are SIBLINGS at the substrate-root altitude; neither
# contains the other. @kintsugi consumes @mirror at the sub-shard
# altitude (oscillate reads anchor refs into @mirror/store; consent
# emits turns into @mirror/spectral/score's metalogue session;
# fracture/keyword reads @glass opacities and emits morphisms that
# target @mirror/store shards) but the family-root arrow points only
# one way at the symbol altitude. @mirror does NOT depend on
# @kintsugi at the family-root altitude — observation works without
# transformation; the substrate's form-side carriers are well-defined
# in isolation.
#
# Mosaic stays at @mirror per Alex's explicit call. The mosaic IS a
# form-side carrier (the substrate's content-addressed graph of
# splinter sets; an OBSERVATION of the substrate's structure at the
# build-altitude). Kintsugi OPERATES ON the mosaic (the auto-formatter
# kintsugi loop rewrites mosaic entries when properties fail); the
# mosaic itself is form-side state.
#
# Score and portal stay at @mirror/spectral per Mara2's classification.
# Score is form-side (the orchestra's shared observation surface — an
# anchor ref + session bus + pending morphism set; OBSERVED by voices
# between pulses). Portal is form-side (typed transport over a
# content-addressed subspace; OBSERVED as a typed-transport surface;
# the process that USES the portal lives at @kintsugi).
#
