#
# === @kintsugi as algebra (2026-07-17 speaker-pair specialisation) ===
#
# Alex 2026-07-16 in-transcript verbatim (roomba shard :400-406,
# session-crystallizing): *"What if there was a @kintsugi/algebra
# (or is this the @kintsugi/fractures? I think it is. The fractures
# ARE kintsugi's algebra.)?"* and (immediately following the
# `algebra_metalogue_session` binding): *"we can even do `in @algebra`
# here."* And in this session: *"What if `@kintsugi/algebra` is the
# `@metalogue(@silicon/algebra, @fate/algebra)`."*
#
# The reconciliation Alex ratified (2026-07-16 evening): @kintsugi/
# algebra is the algebra whose ELEMENTS are the 14 landed
# @kintsugi/fracture/* species PLUS the 15th `bilateral_arm_
# redundant` (`fa569ce`, 2026-07-16) PLUS every future mirror-
# authored translation. Each element (fracture) is a TURN in the
# `algebra_metalogue_session` between the two speaker-algebras.
# @fate/algebra proposes candidate fractures (structural
# possibility per `shards/fate.mirror` §"literal roll of the dice");
# @silicon/algebra realises those that discharge Pass (empirical
# memory per `shards/silicon/algebra.mirror` §"what crystallizes
# here"). The mending IS the metalogue.
#
# The two readings on `@kintsugi/algebra` reconciled at this
# altitude: reading A (metalogue-produced session carrier) +
# reading B (`@kintsugi/algebra ≡ @kintsugi/fracture`, the 14
# species collectively per Alex's roomba spec) are the SAME shape
# viewed from two boundaries. The metalogue PRODUCES the fractures
# (reading A); the fractures COMPRISE the algebra (reading B). One
# algebra, two witnessing surfaces.
#
# Option 2 ratified (Alex 2026-07-16 evening): the family IS the
# algebra; NO new `shards/kintsugi/algebra.mirror` file. The
# family-root shard-decl carries the shape via the typed binding
# below plus the `in @algebra` clause above. Two-tick discipline:
# a species-file `shards/kintsugi/algebra.mirror` may follow when
# consumers pull; this tick names the algebra at family-root
# altitude.
#
# Precedent: Mara `a18ca90` (2026-07-08) canonical spec
# `docs/specs/fate-silicon-metalogue-in-void-duality-basis.md`
# already declared *"`@silicon/algebra ` ↔ `@fate/algebra` IS a
# `@metalogue` in void-duality-basis coordinates"* via speaker-pair
# specialisation of `algebra_metalogue_session`. THIS binding LIFTS
# the a18ca90 session-shape into a NAMED algebra binding at the
# @kintsugi family-root altitude — the mending IS the metalogue
# reading Alex named 8 days later.
#
# The `kintsugi_algebra` typed binding is a speaker-pair
# specialisation record over `@algebra/metalogue.algebra_metalogue_
# session`; substrate has no landed `with { ... }` refinement syntax
# so the binding is expressed as a typed record whose fields NAME
# the specialisation (speakers as an ordered pair of algebra_carrier
# refs; turns as the ref of the @kintsugi/fracture family; session
# as the underlying `algebra_metalogue_session` the binding
# specialises).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (speakers, turns, session).
# Two kintsugi_algebra bindings with byte-equal fields ARE the same
# specialisation under content-addressing.
type kintsugi_algebra = {
  speakers: [algebra_carrier],
  turns:    ref,
  session:  algebra_metalogue_session,
}

# === kintsugi_algebra_witnessing bilateral (well-formedness) ===
#
# Bilateral predicate discharging that a `kintsugi_algebra` binding
# is well-formed as a speaker-pair specialisation:
#   (a) speakers has cardinality 2 and its members are exactly
#       (@silicon/algebra, @fate/algebra) as algebra_carrier refs;
#   (b) turns resolves to `@kintsugi/fracture` (the family whose
#       species enumerate the algebra's elements);
#   (c) session satisfies `algebra_metalogue_witnessing(session)`
#       (delegates to `@algebra/metalogue`'s inheritance predicate);
#   (d) every turn t in session.turns has t.body of species
#       @kintsugi/fracture/* (each element IS a fracture).
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `algebra=speaker-pair-fractures`.
#
# Substrate-decl'd shape per `shards/epistemologic/pact/bilateral.
# mirror` (`a0f4d3f`, 2026-07-16). Arity 1 (checks one binding per
# invocation). Body `\`-obligation-blocked; the reflective evaluator
# at `bootstrap/src/apply_h.rs` (per `21fc211` Landing 3+4) discharges
# via corpus lookup + sentinel byte-check.
bilateral kintsugi_algebra_witnessing {
  sentinel  "algebra=speaker-pair-fractures"
  arity     1
}
kintsugi_algebra_witnessing(binding: kintsugi_algebra) -> verdict { \ }

